[30.050586, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Provider: anthropic-vertex\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Model: claude-haiku-4-5\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Working directory: /tmp/ami-demo-UM6VRF\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Session: session-20261113-134822-889-0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Permissions: auto-allow\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mTip: Run \u001b[1mami --skill <name>\u001b[22m to pin a skill stance for the session.\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Build a small CLI Morse code translator in Python, split across three files in the current \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mdirectory: morse_table.py (the character-to-Morse mapping), encoder.py (text to Morse), decoder.py \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m(Morse back to text), and main.py that imports them all, encodes the phrase 'HELLO WORLD', prints \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mthe Morse, decodes it back, and prints both results so I can see the round-trip works. Run main.py \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mat the end. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll build a Morse code translator CLI for you across three files plus main.py. Let me start by\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kcreating each module.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m[Checkpoint cp-1794574132374-1: /tmp/ami-demo-UM6VRF/morse_table.py]\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[38;5;167m\u25cf\u001b[39m \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;167mfile_edit\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;243m/tmp/ami-demo-UM6VRF/morse_table.py\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;167m